Subject: [PATCH] ctrl: a renew request from the CLI is decoded and renews the radios it names

The CLI's cfg_renew sent its CfgRenew.json, a wfa-dataelements:Renew subdoc, with the bus event
type of the controller's own raw renew (em_bus_event_type_cfg_renew_params_t: a radio, or the
null MAC for every radio). The controller read the subdoc's name as that radio ("Radio:
43:66:67:52:65:6e" is "CfgRen"): no radio matched, nothing was renewed, the CLI was never
answered (its read timed out) and nothing said why.

A renew request now has its own bus event type, em_bus_event_type_cfg_renew_subdoc. The CLI
sends the caller's tree (as set_ssid and set_policy do) or else the CfgRenew.json file. The
controller decodes the Renew object: each DeviceList entry names an agent by its AL MAC ("ID"),
each of its RadioList entries one radio by its current operating class (CurrentOperatingClasses,
one Class), and each radio gets its own cfg_renew command, as the raw renew of one radio. The
whole request is checked first: one that is not such an object, an agent the controller does not
know, a class that matches no current class of the agent's radios (or more than one), or more
than EM_MAX_CMD radios refuses it, logged, and nothing is renewed. The CLI is answered: Success,
Error_Invalid_Input for a refused request, or Error_Not_Ready.

The raw renew is taken only at its own size: anything else is refused, logged, never read as a
radio MAC. The orchestrator's renew of a radio whose configuration was cancelled now sets that
size (it left data_len unset). The controller's own renews are unchanged: the null-MAC renew of
every radio at start, the cancelled radio's renew, and set_ssid's and the onboarding SSID
mismatch's renews.

Platform-independent.

Upstream-Status: Pending

